NOTE ON RESPONSIBLE USE

Sahara is a prototype addressing domestic violence support. It is NOT a
substitute for professional crisis services and has not undergone the safety
review required for real-world deployment to survivors. Anyone reusing this
code for a survivor-facing service must first conduct safety red-teaming,
obtain expert review of risk-assessment logic, implement privacy hardening and
applicable data-protection compliance, and provide trained human escalation.
The legal content reflects Indian law as summarised for this project and must
be verified by a qualified lawyer before any real use.
